{"name":"Ranch House","hex":"#7b645a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ranch house","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of ranchhouse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ranch_house"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ranch-style house","blocks":[{"text":"Ranch is a domestic architectural style that originated in the United States. The ranch-style house is noted for its long, close-to-the-ground profile, and wide open layout. The style fused modernist ideas and styles with notions of the American Western period of wide open spaces to create a very informal and casual living style. While the original ranch style was informal and basic in design, ranch-style houses built in the United States from around the early 1960s increasingly had more dramatic features such as varying roof lines, cathedral ceilings, sunken living rooms, and extensive landscaping and grounds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/HouseII2007.jpg/330px-HouseII2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranch-style_house","wikidata":"Q2130555"},{"title":"Ranch","blocks":[{"text":"A ranch is an area of land, including various structures, given primarily to ranching, the practice of raising grazing livestock such as cattle and sheep. It is a subtype of farm. These terms are most often applied to livestock-raising operations in Mexico, the Western United States and Western Canada, though there are ranches in other areas. People who own or operate a ranch are called ranchers, cattlemen, or stockgrowers. Ranching is also a method used to raise less common livestock such as horses, elk, American bison, ostrich, emu, and alpaca."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Grant-Kohrs_Ranch.jpg/330px-Grant-Kohrs_Ranch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranch","wikidata":"Q509028"},{"title":"House","blocks":[{"text":"A house is a residential building. It may range in complexity from a rudimentary hut to a complex structure of wood, masonry, concrete or other material, outfitted with plumbing, electrical, and heating, ventilation, and air conditioning systems. Houses use a range of different roofing systems to keep precipitation such as rain from getting into the dwelling space. Houses generally have doors or locks to secure the dwelling space and protect its inhabitants and contents from burglars or other trespassers. Most conventional modern houses in Western cultures will contain one or more bedrooms and bathrooms, a kitchen or cooking area, and a living room. A house may have a separate dining room, or the eating area may be integrated into the kitchen or another room. Some large houses in North America have a recreation room. In traditional agriculture-oriented societies, domestic animals such as chickens or larger livestock may share part of the house with humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Katsura_Imperial_Villa_in_Spring.jpg/330px-Katsura_Imperial_Villa_in_Spring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House","wikidata":"Q3947"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/RamblerHouse.JPG/500px-RamblerHouse.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/RamblerHouse.JPG/500px-RamblerHouse.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Smaller ranch-style house in West Jordan, Utah, with brick exterior and side drop gable roof","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARamblerHouse.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/1950s_Ranch-style_House_California.jpg/500px-1950s_Ranch-style_House_California.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/1950s_Ranch-style_House_California.jpg/1280px-1950s_Ranch-style_House_California.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/1950s_Ranch-style_House_California.jpg/500px-1950s_Ranch-style_House_California.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1950s ranch house with dovecote","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1950s_Ranch-style_House_California.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Wideeaves.JPG/500px-Wideeaves.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Wideeaves.JPG/1280px-Wideeaves.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Wideeaves.JPG/500px-Wideeaves.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wide eaves of a typical ranch house, this one built in 1966 in California","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWideeaves.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Ranchsupermarket.JPG/500px-Ranchsupermarket.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Ranchsupermarket.JPG/1280px-Ranchsupermarket.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Ranchsupermarket.JPG/500px-Ranchsupermarket.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Former supermarket in ranch style","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARanchsupermarket.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi